ulti-ticket autodev runs.\n194\t\n195\t### 3. Rerun failed workflow (P0)\n196\t\n197\tAfter cleanup + `.dockerignore` fix:\n198\t```bash\n199\tgh workflow run 'Main CI + Deploy QA' --ref main\n200\t```\n201\t\n202\tOr manual trigger from Actions UI.\n203\t\n204\t**Expected outcome:** Build succeeds with freed disk space + pruned build context.\n205\t\n206\t### 4. Verify QA deploy health (P1)\n207\t\n208\tOnce workflow succeeds:\n209\t```bash\n210\tcurl -s https://qa.fedes.dev/health | jq\n211\t```\n212\t\n213\tExpect:\n214\t```json\n215\t{\n216\t  \"status\": \"healthy\",\n217\t  \"version\": \"...\",\n218\t  \"commit\": \"e273f215...\"\n219\t}\n220\t```\n221\t\n222\t---\n223\t\n224\t## Anomalies (Non-Blocking)\n225\t\n226\t### GitHub Actions Telegram notification defect (known)\n227\t\n228\t**Symptom:** `Notify Telegram on success` step in CI job reported `success`, but no Telegram delivery actually happened.\n229\t\n230\t**Evidence:**\n231\t```json\n232\t{\n233\t  \"name\": \"Notify Telegram on success\",\n234\t  \"conclusion\": \"success\",\n235\t  \"status\": \"completed\"\n236\t}\n237\t```\n238\t\n239\tNo corresponding message received in Telegram (expected format: \"✅ CI passed — fscheu/QuantAgent main@e273f215\").\n240\t\n241\t**Classification:** Known non-blocking GitHub Actions notification bug; does not affect deploy logic or health.\n242\t\n243\t**Reference:** `~/.hermes/skills/fede/tech-lead-autodev/references/qa-deploy-notification-anomalies.md`\n244\t\n245\t**Resolution:** This is a GitHub Actions/notification integration quirk; not a code regression. Monitor for pattern escalation; no immediate action required.\n246\t\n247\t---\n248\t\n249\t## Decision\n250\t\n251\t**Do NOT treat this as a code regression.**\n252\t\n253\tThis is a **self-hosted runner capacity exhaustion** triggered by:\n254\t1. Docker image bloat (24.67 GB reclaimable but not pruned)\n255\t2. Build context bloat (1.3 GB `.worktrees/` not excluded from COPY)\n256\t3. 94% root disk usa